menu "WiSense CSI receiver"

    config WISENSE_CSI_STREAM_BINARY
        bool "Stream raw CSI frames over USB"
        default y if !WISENSE_CLASSIFIER_TINYML
        default n
        help
            Emits the binary CSI frames that python/capture/capture_csi_binary.py
            and the dataset collection scripts read. Required for capturing
            training data or running the PC-side live detector.

            Turn it off when the on-device model is doing the classifying: the
            frames and ESP_LOG output share the one USB-Serial-JTAG peripheral,
            so ~100 binary frames a second make the console unreadable in
            idf.py monitor. Default follows the classifier backend for that
            reason.

endmenu
